<div class="section--tight container">
<div class="prose reveal"><p>We started Aura &amp; Oak in 2019 in a converted garage in Portland, Oregon, with one candle — Amber &amp; Oakmoss — and a stubborn belief that the things we smell every day should be made with as much care as the things we eat.</p><p>Seven years later, we're still a small studio. We still pour by hand. We're still obsessed with the way a scent can make a room feel like home.</p></div>
<div class="timeline reveal">
<div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-year">2019</div><h3>The garage</h3><p>First candle poured. Sold at a local farmers' market to twelve people who believed.</p></div>
<div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-year">2020</div><h3>The studio</h3><p>Moved into a proper studio in the Alberta Arts District. Hired our first pourer.</p></div>
<div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-year">2022</div><h3>The vessels</h3><p>Began working with local ceramicists to create refillable, hand-thrown vessels.</p></div>
<div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-year">2024</div><h3>The diffusers</h3><p>Launched our ceramic reed diffuser line — our most sustainable system yet.</p></div>
<div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-year">2026</div><h3>Today</h3><p>A team of nine, still pouring every candle by hand. Still obsessed with the ritual.</p></div>
</div>
<blockquote class="founder-quote reveal">"We don't make candles for rooms. We make candles for the moment you walk into a room and exhale."<cite>— Elena Voss, Founder</cite></blockquote>
<div class="values-grid stagger">
<div class="value"><h4>Small batch</h4><p>Every candle poured by hand in Portland. No outsourcing, ever.</p></div>
<div class="value"><h4>Slow design</h4><p>We take a year to develop a scent. Some take two.</p></div>
<div class="value"><h4>Refillable</h4><p>Vessels designed to outlive the candle inside them.</p></div>
<div class="value"><h4>Transparent</h4><p>We list every ingredient. No secrets, no greenwashing.</p></div>
</div></div>
